1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} At the time of Anna’s birth her parents lived at Nokkerud, Degernes, where her father was a farmer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna was 13 years old in 1900 when her father re-married and she got to live with a young farmer and his wife at the farm Lilleheier in Degernes, Norway. She was old enough to help out on the farm and in the house. The young coupl
2 CONC e got many children, one after another.  Because of this, Anna had to work in the barn, starting at 5:00 AM, before walking the long distance from Lilleheier to Sandbek School (close to Greaker).  Anna lived with the farmers at Li
2 CONC lleheier for 5 years, and worked for free until she turned 18 in 1905.
2 CONT
2 CONT She then worked as maid/farmhelp on the farm Sølvskutt in Degernes, where she stayed for the next 2 years, 1905-1907.
2 CONT
2 CONT She left Sølvskutt and got work as maid/farmhelp on the large farm Storetorp. This is where she met Kristian who had left his home and family as a teen-ager looking for work.  So – this is where Anna Dingtorp from Degernes and Kri
2 CONC stian Pinås from Tune met. Kristian later got a job at Borregaard, Sarpsborg as a locomotive operator.
2 CONT
2 CONT They married in 1908. Anna and Kristian’s Wedding was held at Pinaas on October 11, 1908.  Dora Bjørnland attended who made and served good food and coffee. They also had good desert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kristian then bade farewell to Pinaas and moved with his Anna to Lande.
2 CONT
2 CONT The next summer, on June 16, 1909 they got their first baby, a girl, and they named her Martha Kristine.  They got 10 children in all.
