1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Notes: (from www.pinaas.no – by Johannes’s daughter Karen Dingtorp) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth's husband Johannes had a difficult time after his wife 1st wife Maren’s death. He had 5 young children that all needed attention. He could not afford to hire a housekeeper, so he went looking for a new wife. He got in to
2 CONC uch with a 30 year old lady, Elise Stentorp, and they got married. Elise agreed to the marriage providing that she did not have to raise his children, so Johannes had to get rid of his children somehow. However – Elise was willing
2 CONC  to keep one child, and it was Karen that got to stay. (The other 4 kids was placed with other families in the community)
2 CONT
2 CONT My stepmother Elise was strict, difficult and not very nice to me. She was strong, something I felt when she beat me. What was most difficult for me to handle was that she did not speak the truth to my father about us children. Sh
2 CONC e made sure that my father did not send any money to any of his other children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
