1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''1886- Birth:'''  Kristian Johansen Pinaas' birth and baptism is recorded in Tune Ministerialbok No 17 (1878-1887) page 161 No 22. His parents lived on Pinaas in Tune where his father was leasing land.  Godparent
2 CONC s were:  Karen Johanne Johannesdatter,  Helene Mortensdatter Holen, Johan Peter Jensen, Karsten Jensen Pinaas, and Hans Martinsen Holen.                                                                                              
2 CONC                                      http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20060920040529.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1900 – Confirmation: '''Kristian Johansen Pinaas’ confirmation is recorded in Tune Ministerialbok No 19 (1898-1904) Page 217 No 29.                                                                                                
2 CONC                                                         http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a1450-kb20060718060207.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1908 – Marriage:'''  Kristian and Anna’s marriage is recorded in Tune Ministerialbok No 20 (1904-1909) Page 288 No 57.  Best men were: Johannes Nilsen Bjørnland and Herman Martinsen Lande. http://www.arkivverket.no/URN:NBN:no-a
2 CONC 1450-kb20060604040289.jpg
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes:'''  (by Jenny Pinaas in Øvre Tune, Østfold, Norway) Kristian left home at a young age and got work as farm helper on the large farm Storetorp in Degernes.  This was where he met his future wife, Anna Dingtorp, who he mar
2 CONC ried in 1908.
2 CONT
2 CONT After they got married, Kristian built their home at Borgenveien 3, Borgenhaugen, Skjeberg.  His grand-daughter Grethe Solberg currently (2013) lives in this house with her family. Kristian worked most of his life at the Borregaar
2 CONC d factory in Sarpsborg, where he worked as a stoker of the factory locomotive. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a religious awakening happening in Degernes at that time and many young people including Kristian and Anna decided to follow Jesus Christ.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kristian had a good friend in Degernes named Sevrin Mellegaard and they started a musical gospel group there.  Kristian became the leader of the group, he played the violin, Sevrin played the guitar, Anna played “harpeleik”, and m
2 CONC any more joined the group.
2 CONT
2 CONT After a while, Kristian brought with him a girl when he visited his home at Pinaas.  And can you guess who this girl was?  Yes – it was Anna, who little-by-little had demanded a place in Kristian’s heart, and now got to keep this 
2 CONC place.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kristian then came ”home” and found work at Borregaard in Saprpsborg.  He married Anna the following year and moved to Lande outside Sarpsborg.  There he started yet another gospel group that still sings today.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna and Kristian’s Wedding was held at Pinaas on October 12, 1908.  Dora Bjørnland attended who made and served good food and coffee.  They also had good desert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kristian then bade farewell to Pinaas and moved with his Anna to Lande.
2 CONT
2 CONT The next summer, on June 16, 1909 they got their first baby, a girl, and they named her Martha Kristine.  They got 10 children in all.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Mentioned here: [http://www.pinaas.no/slekt/pinaas.htm#17] no 32.
