1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Fredrik Joachimsen Borse f. 00-00-1712, Solum, Telemark,
2 CONT
2 CONT     g. 01-08-1737, Østby gård, Skjeberg, Maria Magdalena Juliane von Storm , f. ca. 1719, Skjeberg, (datter av Adolph Carl von Meyer og Elisabeth Augusta von Storm ) d. 1791. Fredrik døde 00-00-1762, Aremark. Fredrik hadde en mill
2 CONC itær løpebane. I Overstadens Militærbiografier heter det bl.a. om denne Fredrik: Han var sjersjant, fenrik, secondløytnant.Tok avskjed året 1741 Han tjenestegjorde ved forskjellige infanteriregimener.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Før giftemålet var han bosatt på Øvre Hornes i Skjeberg. Etter giftemålet flyttet han og familien til Aremark. Bryllupet sto på Østby gård i Skjeberg, den gang en offisergård. I 1747 bodde han på Skotsberg i Aremark og drev 2 
2 CONC små gårder der. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.pinaas.no/slekt/dingtorp.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Fredrik and Maria got married on Østby farm in Skjeberg. Fredrik had a military carier.     In the book ”Overstadens Militærbiografier” it is written that Fredrik was a sergeant, fenrik, secondløytnant. He retired from the army in
2 CONC  1741. Fredrik served at various ”infanteri regimenter”.  He lived at Øvre Hornes in Skjeberg before he got married.  He moved to Aremark with his family after he got married.
2 CONT
2 CONT The wedding was held at Østby farm in Skjeberg, which at that time served as an officer farm for military personnel.  In 1747, Fredrik lived at Skotsberg in Aremark where he managed two small farms, Mosserød and Skotsberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the time of Maria’s confirmation in Kristiansøe Kirke in Skjeberg, she is recorded in the church record with the last name von Meyer. When she got married in 1737 at the approximate age of 18 she is recorded with the last name 
2 CONC von Storm. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As a curiosity;  Maria and Fredrik’s first child was bor the day after their wedding.    Their 4 first children were born in Skjeberg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Fredrik Joachimsen Borsse (1712-1762) had a military career. The book “Overstadens Military Biography” states. He was Sergeant, Ensign, and Second Lieutenant, resigned the year 1741. He served in different infantry regiments. Befo
2 CONC re his marriage, he lived at Øvre Hornes in Skjeberg. After the marriage he moved with the family to Aremark. The wedding was held at Østby gård in Skjeberg, at the time an officer's farm. In 1747 he lived at Skotsberg in Aremark 
2 CONC and ran two small farms there, Mosserød and Skotsberg.
