1 NOTE {geni:about_me} La Verne Margaret Ziemba, 86 of Necedah, passed away on Sunday, May 4, 2008, at St. Joseph's Hospital in Marshfield. She was born on Sept. 29, 1921, to William and Inga (Hoff) Masonberg in Chicago, Ill. She was uni
2 CONC ted in marriage on July 7, 1945, to the love of her life, Stanley Ziemba. For nearly 40 years they made their home in Bellwood, Ill., and shortly after retirement, moved to Necedah. A fastidious homemaker, she took great pride in 
2 CONC keeping her home. La Verne also had a great love for her German shepherd, Duke. She is survived by her husband Stanley of Necedah; many nieces, nephews, other relatives and friends. She was preceded in death by her parents and 12 
2 CONC brothers and sisters. A memorial service will be held on Sunday, May 18, 2008, 1:30 p.m. at the Torkelson Necedah Family Funeral Home in Necedah. Pastor James Link will officiate. In lieu of flowers, donations may be made to the F
2 CONC oundation of St. Joseph's Hospital for the Palliative Care Unit, 611 St. Joseph Ave, Marshfield, WI 54449. The Torkelson Necedah Family Funeral Home is assisting with arrangements. © The County Star-Times, Juneau, WI, 7 May 2008
